# Phase discipline

Read [docs/master-spec.md](docs/master-spec.md) and the current phase doc before changing code.

Work only on the current phase. The current phase is Phase 6. See [docs/phase-6.md](docs/phase-6.md). Phase 1, Phase 2, Phase 3, Phase 4, and Phase 5 are complete.

Feature work happens on `develop`. Merge to `main` only when the user is ready for production.

Phase 6 is exchange connections. Store encrypted, trade-only keys on Live accounts. The model is venue-agnostic; Bybit is the first enabled venue. Do not place exchange orders. Do not add a Fly.io worker. Do not call private exchange APIs from the browser. Paper accounts still use the Phase 4 paper ledger. Live accounts may exist; the tick must not execute them. Paper auto-switch is postponed. Phase 7 (additional exchanges, UI refine, Paper market-data venue picker) is written in [docs/phase-7.md](docs/phase-7.md) — do not start it until Phase 6 is accepted and Bybit connections are confirmed.

Do not create later-phase tables or speculative architecture.

Keep dependencies minimal. Prefer the simplest solution that satisfies the current phase.

Work one micro-step at a time as listed in [docs/phase-6.md](docs/phase-6.md). Stop at the end of each micro-step and wait for instruction.

Stop at the end of the phase. After acceptance criteria pass, report results and wait for instruction.
